  "name": "MEAN CORPUSCULAR VOLUME (MCV)",
  "code": "1567",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>It measures the <strong data-start=\"210\" data-end=\"235\">average size (volume)</strong> of a red blood cell (RBC), measured in femtoliters (fL).</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>MCV Result</th>\n<th>Interpretation</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Low (&lt;80 fL)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Microcytic anemia</strong> &ndash; RBCs are smaller than normal. Common causes: Iron deficiency, Thalassemia, Chronic disease.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normal (80&ndash;100 fL)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Normocytic anemia</strong> &ndash; RBCs are normal in size.Causes: Acute blood loss, anemia of chronic disease, early kidney disease.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>High (&gt;100 fL)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Macrocytic anemia</strong> &ndash; RBCs are larger than normal.Causes: Vitamin B12 or folate deficiency, liver disease, alcoholism, hypothyroidism, certain medications.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
